WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:12.355
Hello, and welcome to Preshift Rota, from Williams, Stanley and Co. and Preshift Rota.

2
00:00:12.355 --> 00:00:15.183
Here's the thing about a rota.

3
00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:18.294
It's where culture and cost meet.

4
00:00:18.294 --> 00:00:23.761
Get it wrong, and your team is run ragged on a busy night.

5
00:00:23.761 --> 00:00:26.495
or padded out on a quiet one.

6
00:00:26.495 --> 00:00:29.606
And the numbers never quite hold.

7
00:00:30.057 --> 00:00:33.624
Preshift Rota sizes every shift to the forecast.

8
00:00:33.624 --> 00:00:40.591
It shares the hard shifts fairly, protects rest, and gets the rota out in good time.

9
00:00:40.591 --> 00:00:46.646
And it costs each shift the way payroll will, so the labour in your P and

10
00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.881
L is right before payroll has even run.

11
00:00:50.331 --> 00:00:54.171
Everything you'll see is the public demo.

12
00:00:54.171 --> 00:00:55.856
Anyone can try it:

13
00:00:55.856 --> 00:01:01.944
two companies, three London sites, with real teams and forecasts.

14
00:01:01.944 --> 00:01:07.094
It's your own private copy, and it's wiped at midnight.

15
00:01:07.094 --> 00:01:08.499
Let's start it.

16
00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:15.243
Every Monday, Preshift Rota offers you that week's changes as a short tour.

17
00:01:15.243 --> 00:01:20.270
One card per change, each opening the screen it changed.

18
00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:22.424
Let's have a quick look.

19
00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:28.432
Next takes you straight to the next change, on its own screen.

20
00:01:28.432 --> 00:01:33.003
Two minutes, and nobody has to read a release note.

21
00:01:33.454 --> 00:01:38.768
You can replay it any time from What's new, top right.

22
00:01:38.768 --> 00:01:42.310
Right, let's close it and get going.

23
00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.998
Everything lives in one bar across the top.

24
00:01:50.998 --> 00:01:55.201
It's grouped the way a GM runs the week.

25
00:01:55.201 --> 00:01:56.042
Plan it.

26
00:01:56.042 --> 00:01:58.774
Run the hours and the pay.

27
00:01:58.774 --> 00:02:00.875
Look after the team.

28
00:02:00.875 --> 00:02:02.872
And then the money.

29
00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:08.855
Open a group, and every section tells you, in a line, what it's for.

30
00:02:08.855 --> 00:02:12.029
People only see what their role allows.

31
00:02:12.029 --> 00:02:18.782
And an owner can switch off whatever the business doesn't use, so a GM isn't wading

32
00:02:18.782 --> 00:02:21.467
through forty screens to use ten.

33
00:02:21.918 --> 00:02:23.950
Looking for something?

34
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:29.310
Press the slash key, type a few letters, and you're there.

35
00:02:29.761 --> 00:02:32.811
Your own menu sits top right.

36
00:02:32.811 --> 00:02:39.121
In the demo, it lets you see Preshift Rota as anyone on the team.

37
00:02:39.121 --> 00:02:41.960
A GM, a supervisor, a chef.

38
00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:46.693
Each one sees exactly what their role allows.

39
00:02:46.693 --> 00:02:48.481
and nothing more.

40
00:02:48.932 --> 00:02:53.088
And down in the corner, there's Ask Shifty.

41
00:02:53.088 --> 00:02:57.052
Ask it a question, or tell it what to do.

42
00:02:57.052 --> 00:02:59.372
We'll come back to that.

43
00:03:03.542 --> 00:03:08.649
Under every heading, there's one line of numbers.

44
00:03:08.649 --> 00:03:13.651
Labour as a share of sales, against your target.

45
00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:14.276
Sales.

46
00:03:14.276 --> 00:03:15.006
Labour.

47
00:03:15.006 --> 00:03:18.549
How far inside the budget you are.

48
00:03:18.549 --> 00:03:23.030
And anything that needs a compliance check.

49
00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.170
Want the detail?

50
00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:29.711
Full P and L opens the statement behind it.

51
00:03:29.711 --> 00:03:33.090
Wages, holiday, N I and pension.

52
00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:37.208
right down to what's left after labour.

53
00:03:37.658 --> 00:03:40.933
Below that, every site side by side.

54
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:44.753
You can see straight away who's on target.

55
00:03:44.753 --> 00:03:46.027
and who isn't.

56
00:03:46.027 --> 00:03:52.394
And a site with a problem that blocks publishing says so, right there.

57
00:03:52.844 --> 00:03:56.460
Further down, there's travel between sites.

58
00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:03.271
Journey times come from T f L, so nobody gets rostered across London with no time

59
00:04:03.271 --> 00:04:04.364
to get there.

60
00:04:04.814 --> 00:04:09.966
And one press of Build from forecast builds every site at once.

61
00:04:09.966 --> 00:04:12.173
Each site's own team first.

62
00:04:12.173 --> 00:04:16.670
then cover from people who've agreed to work elsewhere.

63
00:04:20.842 --> 00:04:22.478
Let's open a site.

64
00:04:22.478 --> 00:04:24.204
This is Marylebone.

65
00:04:24.204 --> 00:04:30.564
Same line of numbers at the top, so the cost of the week is never more

66
00:04:30.564 --> 00:04:32.290
than a glance away.

67
00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.667
Coming up tells you what's ahead.

68
00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:36.909
Bonfire Night.

69
00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:43.915
And a corporate function, still provisional, forty standing in the garden room.

70
00:04:43.915 --> 00:04:48.172
You'll want that on your radar before you build.

71
00:04:48.623 --> 00:04:51.842
Then the decisions, most urgent first.

72
00:04:51.842 --> 00:04:56.163
Each one tells you what's wrong, what it's costing.

73
00:04:56.163 --> 00:04:59.805
and gives you the one button that fixes it.

74
00:04:59.805 --> 00:05:03.617
Here, someone's below their contracted hours.

75
00:05:03.617 --> 00:05:09.377
You're paying for those hours anyway, so give them the shifts first.

76
00:05:09.377 --> 00:05:12.935
It's fairer for them, and cheaper for you.

77
00:05:13.384 --> 00:05:17.243
Across the week, there are day notes.

78
00:05:17.243 --> 00:05:19.642
A delivery to check in.

79
00:05:19.642 --> 00:05:23.083
Allergen training before service.

80
00:05:23.083 --> 00:05:26.212
The bay closed for road works.

81
00:05:26.212 --> 00:05:30.592
Everyone sees them, right where they plan.

82
00:05:31.043 --> 00:05:33.373
And here's the timeline.

83
00:05:33.373 --> 00:05:37.160
Each day sits over its own sales curve.

84
00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:44.247
The shifts are bars, front of house, bar and kitchen, each with its cost.

85
00:05:44.247 --> 00:05:50.363
The strip underneath shows where you're short, in red, or over.

86
00:05:50.814 --> 00:05:53.894
And you choose how much you see.

87
00:05:53.894 --> 00:06:00.054
Simple is just the decisions and the timeline, the calm version.

88
00:06:00.054 --> 00:06:02.846
Standard adds the main views.

89
00:06:02.846 --> 00:06:05.445
Expert lays everything out.

90
00:06:05.445 --> 00:06:09.198
Each person picks, and it's remembered.

91
00:06:13.374 --> 00:06:14.724
Now, next week.

92
00:06:14.724 --> 00:06:19.404
Nothing's built yet, and the first decision says so:

93
00:06:19.404 --> 00:06:24.174
thirty eight thousand pounds of sales, and nobody on.

94
00:06:24.174 --> 00:06:29.394
So, rather than copying last week and hoping for the best.

95
00:06:29.394 --> 00:06:32.094
we build it from the forecast.

96
00:06:32.545 --> 00:06:38.979
It works out how many people each hour needs, gives hours to anyone below their contract

97
00:06:38.979 --> 00:06:44.682
first, then fills the gaps with the cheapest person who can legally work them.

98
00:06:44.682 --> 00:06:45.121
Watch.

99
00:06:45.572 --> 00:06:46.077
Done.

100
00:06:46.077 --> 00:06:49.416
Costed, legal, and inside budget.

101
00:06:49.416 --> 00:06:53.665
And it's honest about what it couldn't do.

102
00:06:53.665 --> 00:06:58.622
Some gaps can't be filled legally with this team.

103
00:06:58.622 --> 00:07:02.972
That's a hiring signal, not a rota problem.

104
00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.818
This is my favourite part.

105
00:07:05.818 --> 00:07:08.029
Coaching for this draft.

106
00:07:08.029 --> 00:07:12.083
Preshift Rota remembers how your past weeks went.

107
00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:18.625
So it says, Monday's over target again, just like the last two Mondays.

108
00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:26.365
Or, three bartenders on together on Friday afternoon, when you only need two, again.

109
00:07:26.365 --> 00:07:32.538
It's like having an operations director looking over your shoulder.

110
00:07:32.538 --> 00:07:33.183
kindly.

111
00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:37.018
When you're happy, Sign off and publish.

112
00:07:37.018 --> 00:07:43.871
Anything that breaks the law blocks it, so nothing illegal ever reaches the team.

113
00:07:43.871 --> 00:07:48.610
And everyone hears about their own shifts, in good time.

114
00:07:52.776 --> 00:07:55.173
Click any shift to open it.

115
00:07:55.173 --> 00:08:01.388
The number that matters is what this shift actually adds to your week.

116
00:08:01.388 --> 00:08:07.426
Marco's on forty guaranteed hours, and he's been given twenty eight.

117
00:08:07.426 --> 00:08:09.113
So this shift adds.

118
00:08:09.113 --> 00:08:09.823
nothing.

119
00:08:09.823 --> 00:08:13.464
You're paying for those hours either way.

120
00:08:13.914 --> 00:08:16.734
And the law is checked as you type.

121
00:08:16.734 --> 00:08:23.179
Cut the break too short, and it tells you, there and then, what the Working Time

122
00:08:23.179 --> 00:08:24.066
rules need.

123
00:08:24.516 --> 00:08:25.494
Now Chloe.

124
00:08:25.494 --> 00:08:30.290
She's paid by the hour, with no guaranteed hours.

125
00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.422
So her shift adds its full cost.

126
00:08:33.422 --> 00:08:38.022
Her pay, her holiday, employer N I and pension.

127
00:08:38.022 --> 00:08:45.852
It's worked out across her whole week, so the rota matches payroll to the penny.

128
00:08:46.303 --> 00:08:50.783
You can work straight on the timeline, too.

129
00:08:50.783 --> 00:08:53.283
Drag a shift to move it.

130
00:08:53.283 --> 00:08:57.034
Or drag the end to change the hours.

131
00:08:57.034 --> 00:09:00.889
Here, Sofia finishes an hour earlier.

132
00:09:00.889 --> 00:09:04.015
Watch the cost update as I go.

133
00:09:04.466 --> 00:09:05.436
Need cover?

134
00:09:05.436 --> 00:09:10.287
Click a red hour, and Preshift Rota asks who should work it.

135
00:09:10.287 --> 00:09:15.315
It ranks people who are trained and free, cheapest first.

136
00:09:15.315 --> 00:09:21.578
And it offers your other sites too, with the reason anyone can't do it.

137
00:09:25.743 --> 00:09:32.669
By person shows everyone's week as a grid, with their hours against their contract.

138
00:09:32.669 --> 00:09:36.423
Drag a shift to someone else, or another day.

139
00:09:36.874 --> 00:09:42.961
The Gantt gives each person a line, with their shifts against the clock.

140
00:09:42.961 --> 00:09:46.258
The whole week, or one day by the hour.

141
00:09:46.709 --> 00:09:49.424
The rest live under More views.

142
00:09:49.424 --> 00:09:56.517
Cover map puts the whole week against demand, so you can see exactly where to add

143
00:09:56.517 --> 00:09:57.218
an hour.

144
00:09:57.218 --> 00:09:58.181
or cut one.

145
00:09:58.631 --> 00:10:02.267
Rest shows each person across two weeks.

146
00:10:02.267 --> 00:10:09.537
So a late close followed by an early open jumps out, before it becomes a breach,

147
00:10:09.537 --> 00:10:10.991
or a tired team.

148
00:10:11.442 --> 00:10:15.173
Positions shows one day by station.

149
00:10:15.173 --> 00:10:20.610
Who's on the bar, the pass, the door, hour by hour.

150
00:10:21.061 --> 00:10:27.070
Shift cost stacks every shift at its true cost against the day's target.

151
00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:32.077
When labour runs over, this is where you decide what to cut.

152
00:10:32.528 --> 00:10:39.392
Changes shows who the next publish will tell, and what, before anyone's told.

153
00:10:39.986 --> 00:10:43.579
And Fairness looks back four weeks.

154
00:10:43.579 --> 00:10:46.863
Weekends, closes, late finishes.

155
00:10:46.863 --> 00:10:50.353
Who keeps getting the hard shifts?

156
00:10:50.353 --> 00:10:54.458
A fair rota is how you keep good people.

157
00:10:54.909 --> 00:10:56.097
Nine views.

158
00:10:56.097 --> 00:10:57.069
One week.

159
00:10:57.069 --> 00:11:03.333
And the How to guide tells you which order to use them in.

160
00:11:07.542 --> 00:11:12.795
Ask the assistant lets you say what you need, in plain English.

161
00:11:12.795 --> 00:11:17.798
Ben's off Saturday, cover the bar without going over target.

162
00:11:17.798 --> 00:11:23.468
It drafts the week using the same costing and the same legal checks.

163
00:11:23.468 --> 00:11:27.054
So it simply can't roster anything illegal.

164
00:11:27.505 --> 00:11:32.314
Nothing changes until you've looked at the draft and said yes.

165
00:11:32.314 --> 00:11:38.209
It's switched off in this public demo, but on your own account it runs live.

166
00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:44.144
And Ask Shifty, in the corner, or Control K from anywhere.

167
00:11:44.144 --> 00:11:47.642
Ask it, who's working Saturday night?

168
00:11:47.642 --> 00:11:50.195
Are we on target this week?

169
00:11:50.195 --> 00:11:53.031
Or tell it, add a new starter.

170
00:11:53.031 --> 00:12:00.500
Every change comes back as a card, and nothing happens until you press confirm.

171
00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:09.410
Your team asks in the staff app, and you decide here.

172
00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.534
Holiday, time off, swaps, sickness.

173
00:12:12.534 --> 00:12:19.674
Every request is checked again when you say yes, so a swap that breaks the rules

174
00:12:19.674 --> 00:12:21.816
simply can't go through.

175
00:12:22.267 --> 00:12:24.571
Need to put a shift out?

176
00:12:24.571 --> 00:12:30.619
Pick it, and Preshift Rota shows everyone who could legally take it.

177
00:12:30.619 --> 00:12:34.651
Cheapest first, with what each would cost.

178
00:12:34.651 --> 00:12:37.339
And why everyone else can't.

179
00:12:37.794 --> 00:12:41.083
You choose who hears about it.

180
00:12:41.083 --> 00:12:46.676
Everyone at once, or the cheapest first, in rounds.

181
00:12:46.676 --> 00:12:48.430
And who decides.

182
00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.500
You, or the first legal yes.

183
00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:56.106
Staff can even just reply yes on WhatsApp.

184
00:12:56.556 --> 00:12:59.598
Or let claims approve themselves.

185
00:12:59.598 --> 00:13:05.038
Only when they break no rule, and the week stays on target.

186
00:13:05.038 --> 00:13:07.620
Anything else waits for you.

187
00:13:11.792 --> 00:13:15.344
The forecast comes from your own till.

188
00:13:15.344 --> 00:13:19.926
The same day and hour, over the last eight weeks.

189
00:13:19.926 --> 00:13:24.320
Recent weeks count most, with the trend on top.

190
00:13:24.771 --> 00:13:29.330
And you can tell it what it can't know.

191
00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.617
A heatwave.

192
00:13:30.617 --> 00:13:33.189
A match down the road.

193
00:13:33.189 --> 00:13:34.124
A refit.

194
00:13:34.124 --> 00:13:37.515
Just add it, with the reason.

195
00:13:37.966 --> 00:13:44.721
Demand turns that into how many people you need, role by role, hour by hour.

196
00:13:44.721 --> 00:13:47.921
So a busy night is staffed properly.

197
00:13:47.921 --> 00:13:50.854
and a quiet one isn't padded out.

198
00:13:51.304 --> 00:13:56.220
The calendar has the whole UK trading year built in.

199
00:13:56.220 --> 00:14:02.081
Bank holidays, Mother's Day, Bonfire Night, Christmas parties.

200
00:14:02.081 --> 00:14:06.808
Plus the weather, local events, and your bookings.

201
00:14:07.259 --> 00:14:13.604
Weddings, buyouts and private functions land here too, and on the rota's demand.

202
00:14:13.604 --> 00:14:20.425
A provisional booking shows as provisional, so you can plan for it without committing.

203
00:14:20.425 --> 00:14:23.915
And each item tells you what to do about it.

204
00:14:28.089 --> 00:14:35.804
Coach finds the three changes that save the most, without leaving the floor short or breaking

205
00:14:35.804 --> 00:14:36.385
a rule.

206
00:14:36.385 --> 00:14:39.040
Trim an edge that's overstaffed.

207
00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:41.528
Take off a shift nobody needs.

208
00:14:41.528 --> 00:14:45.345
Or give a shift to someone cheaper who's free.

209
00:14:45.797 --> 00:14:51.733
Each one shows the saving, and where labour lands afterwards.

210
00:14:51.733 --> 00:14:54.653
Take it, and the rota changes.

211
00:14:55.103 --> 00:14:57.517
And below, the ladder.

212
00:14:57.517 --> 00:14:58.834
Four habits.

213
00:14:58.834 --> 00:15:02.347
The rota out on time, and legal.

214
00:15:02.347 --> 00:15:04.212
Labour on target.

215
00:15:04.212 --> 00:15:08.054
Getting each part of the day right.

216
00:15:08.054 --> 00:15:10.688
And owning the forecast.

217
00:15:10.688 --> 00:15:16.176
A site that hits target with a late rota is lucky.

218
00:15:16.176 --> 00:15:17.603
not well run.

219
00:15:17.603 --> 00:15:22.103
Coach the habits, and the results follow.

220
00:15:26.268 --> 00:15:32.327
Clock in turns a tablet by the staff door into a sign-in point.

221
00:15:32.327 --> 00:15:35.309
Tap a card, or sign in by name.

222
00:15:35.309 --> 00:15:38.964
It shows who's on today, and who's in.

223
00:15:39.415 --> 00:15:44.291
A shared iPad can become a kiosk that does nothing else.

224
00:15:44.291 --> 00:15:50.908
And on the live product, staff can clock in by touching their own phone to a

225
00:15:50.908 --> 00:15:52.301
tag at the door.

226
00:15:52.301 --> 00:15:53.695
No card, no app.

227
00:15:54.145 --> 00:15:57.011
Cut call is for the middle of service.

228
00:15:57.011 --> 00:16:03.121
It compares what you've taken so far with the forecast, and works out the rest of

229
00:16:03.121 --> 00:16:04.705
the day at that pace.

230
00:16:05.157 --> 00:16:11.400
If trade's slow, it tells you who to send home, and exactly what that saves on

231
00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.041
payroll.

232
00:16:12.041 --> 00:16:18.524
And it keeps an eye on who keeps getting sent home, so nobody quietly loses their

233
00:16:18.524 --> 00:16:19.005
hours.

234
00:16:23.175 --> 00:16:28.087
Payroll is five steps, straight through to TeamPay.

235
00:16:28.087 --> 00:16:33.963
In the demo, it's a simulator, so we can run the whole thing.

236
00:16:33.963 --> 00:16:37.239
First, the team goes into TeamPay.

237
00:16:37.691 --> 00:16:40.328
Then the clocked hours.

238
00:16:40.328 --> 00:16:42.851
We'll simulate a week.

239
00:16:43.302 --> 00:16:48.943
Anyone whose break was too short gets flagged, before you approve.

240
00:16:48.943 --> 00:16:53.046
So nobody's quietly working through their break.

241
00:16:53.497 --> 00:16:54.757
Then approve.

242
00:16:54.757 --> 00:17:02.897
If a break was short, Preshift Rota stops you first, and walks you through what to check.

243
00:17:02.897 --> 00:17:05.901
Then send the hours to TeamPay.

244
00:17:05.901 --> 00:17:08.809
It never sends anything twice.

245
00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:15.080
And when the pay run comes back, it's checked against what the rota said.

246
00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:18.908
So finance can see any difference straight away.

247
00:17:23.077 --> 00:17:31.128
Clocked versus rota shows where the hours went differently from the plan.

248
00:17:31.128 --> 00:17:32.452
Late starts.

249
00:17:32.452 --> 00:17:34.106
Early finishes.

250
00:17:34.106 --> 00:17:35.099
Overruns.

251
00:17:35.099 --> 00:17:38.077
Before anything's approved.

252
00:17:38.527 --> 00:17:43.407
Tronc shares out the tips and service charge on hours worked.

253
00:17:43.407 --> 00:17:47.327
So whoever stayed for the close gets paid for it.

254
00:17:47.327 --> 00:17:52.927
And it shows the National Insurance saved, and when it has to be paid.

255
00:17:53.378 --> 00:17:55.789
Pay periods runs the close.

256
00:17:55.789 --> 00:18:03.650
Lock the rota, approve the time cards, and pass the hours to payroll before the cut-off.

257
00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.788
And pay approvals.

258
00:18:05.788 --> 00:18:12.635
Change anyone's rate, and it's only a proposal until finance approves it.

259
00:18:12.635 --> 00:18:15.355
Nobody can approve their own.

260
00:18:15.355 --> 00:18:20.420
And you see the full cost of the change, for the year.

261
00:18:24.583 --> 00:18:30.401
HR overview puts everything you need to act on in one list.

262
00:18:30.401 --> 00:18:32.866
A licence that's expired.

263
00:18:32.866 --> 00:18:35.332
A contract nobody signed.

264
00:18:35.332 --> 00:18:39.967
A return to work chat that hasn't happened yet.

265
00:18:40.418 --> 00:18:43.226
Staff holds everyone's record.

266
00:18:43.226 --> 00:18:45.940
Contract, pay, right to work.

267
00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:50.433
And it's checked before anyone reaches the rota.

268
00:18:50.433 --> 00:18:58.202
No right to work, or pay below the minimum wage, and they simply can't be rostered.

269
00:18:58.652 --> 00:19:03.260
Open a person, and their whole file is right here.

270
00:19:06.325 --> 00:19:11.254
Messages gives each person one thread with their managers.

271
00:19:11.254 --> 00:19:14.738
Plus announcements, with who's read them.

272
00:19:14.738 --> 00:19:17.797
Everything about work, in one place.

273
00:19:17.797 --> 00:19:21.877
not scattered across everyone's WhatsApp groups.

274
00:19:22.328 --> 00:19:27.634
And onboarding gives every new starter one checklist.

275
00:19:27.634 --> 00:19:30.637
The legal bits before day one.

276
00:19:30.637 --> 00:19:32.640
Payroll in week one.

277
00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.443
Training in the first month.

278
00:19:35.443 --> 00:19:39.248
A good first month is how people stay.

279
00:19:43.418 --> 00:19:50.698
Wellbeing looks at the last month, and the fortnight ahead, for every person.

280
00:19:50.698 --> 00:19:51.738
Long weeks.

281
00:19:51.738 --> 00:19:53.157
No weekend off.

282
00:19:53.157 --> 00:19:56.277
A late close then an early start.

283
00:19:56.277 --> 00:19:58.735
None of it breaks the law.

284
00:19:58.735 --> 00:20:03.746
but each one's a conversation worth having this week.

285
00:20:04.197 --> 00:20:10.917
Holiday tracks everyone's allowance, and flags anyone who hasn't had a proper break.

286
00:20:11.368 --> 00:20:18.742
Absence records sickness, and reminds you of every return to work chat you haven't had.

287
00:20:18.742 --> 00:20:22.047
It's the kindest way to manage absence.

288
00:20:22.047 --> 00:20:23.488
and the cheapest.

289
00:20:23.939 --> 00:20:28.778
Training shows every certificate each role needs.

290
00:20:28.778 --> 00:20:32.234
Food hygiene, allergens, licensing.

291
00:20:32.234 --> 00:20:36.875
So you know what an inspector would find today.

292
00:20:37.326 --> 00:20:45.435
Probation and reviews makes sure no probation runs out by accident, and no appraisal gets forgotten.

293
00:20:45.435 --> 00:20:51.030
Cases keeps any disciplinary or grievance confidential, step by step.

294
00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:57.129
Retention shows who might be thinking of leaving, and why.

295
00:20:57.129 --> 00:21:00.050
Usually, it's the rota itself.

296
00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:01.609
Sent home early.

297
00:21:01.609 --> 00:21:03.556
Always on the close.

298
00:21:03.556 --> 00:21:09.984
Each one comes with a fix, and what it would cost to replace them.

299
00:21:10.434 --> 00:21:16.714
And employment rights is ready for the new law on zero and low hours contracts.

300
00:21:16.714 --> 00:21:20.212
Pay owed when a shift's cut at short notice.

301
00:21:20.212 --> 00:21:25.458
And offers of guaranteed hours that match what people really work.

302
00:21:29.622 --> 00:21:35.253
Labour cost shows every pound payroll will charge, person by person.

303
00:21:35.253 --> 00:21:40.470
And it flags wherever you're paying for hours you're not using.

304
00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:46.160
Close gives finance the labour accrual journals, ready to post.

305
00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:51.816
Post them at the end of the week, and your P and L shows true labour

306
00:21:51.816 --> 00:21:52.897
from day one.

307
00:21:52.897 --> 00:21:56.640
That's how you close the month in three days.

308
00:21:57.091 --> 00:21:59.487
Reports covers the rest.

309
00:21:59.487 --> 00:22:09.072
GM scorecards, labour trends, cost by role, forecast accuracy, and how close payroll came to the

310
00:22:09.072 --> 00:22:09.571
rota.

311
00:22:10.022 --> 00:22:15.295
Programme is our twelve week labour programme with Williams, Stanley.

312
00:22:15.295 --> 00:22:22.478
Each milestone is proved by your own figures, and the saving is checked against your accounts.

313
00:22:22.929 --> 00:22:27.701
Prime cost puts labour and cost of sales together.

314
00:22:27.701 --> 00:22:31.233
The two costs a site really controls.

315
00:22:31.817 --> 00:22:37.595
Compliance risk puts a price on any breach, the way a tribunal would.

316
00:22:37.595 --> 00:22:43.289
Find it first, put it right for the person, and the penalty shrinks.

317
00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:52.060
And labour cash shows what leaves the bank for your people over the next thirteen weeks.

318
00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:55.275
Pay days, tips, HMRC and pensions.

319
00:22:55.275 --> 00:23:01.988
A big month on the rota means a bigger HMRC bill about six weeks later.

320
00:23:01.988 --> 00:23:04.068
Now you see it coming.

321
00:23:08.232 --> 00:23:12.672
Set-up holds your companies, sites and roles.

322
00:23:12.672 --> 00:23:15.435
Everything else runs off it.

323
00:23:15.435 --> 00:23:23.328
You can even split a site into areas, like front of house, kitchen, or a bakery.

324
00:23:23.779 --> 00:23:27.732
Access decides who can do what, and where.

325
00:23:27.732 --> 00:23:32.155
Nobody can give themselves more than they have.

326
00:23:32.155 --> 00:23:36.578
Setting pay and running payroll are kept apart.

327
00:23:36.578 --> 00:23:39.307
And every change is recorded.

328
00:23:39.758 --> 00:23:45.567
Integrations shows every connection, and whether it's working.

329
00:23:45.567 --> 00:23:49.127
The till, TeamPay, Xero, card readers.

330
00:23:49.127 --> 00:23:55.310
Anything not connected is something someone's still doing by hand.

331
00:23:55.761 --> 00:24:00.634
GDPR keeps track of data requests and their deadlines.

332
00:24:00.634 --> 00:24:04.785
Because your team's data deserves proper care.

333
00:24:05.235 --> 00:24:11.349
Features lets an owner switch off anything the business doesn't use.

334
00:24:11.349 --> 00:24:12.967
Nothing's deleted.

335
00:24:12.967 --> 00:24:16.923
Switch it back on, and it's all still there.

336
00:24:17.374 --> 00:24:24.303
And under Help, there are how to guides for GMs, this walkthrough, and support from your

337
00:24:24.303 --> 00:24:26.902
Williams, Stanley client partner.

338
00:24:29.489 --> 00:24:34.077
And this is the staff app, on everyone's own phone.

339
00:24:34.077 --> 00:24:38.845
Today shows their next shift, and their recent hours.

340
00:24:38.845 --> 00:24:43.433
Where the site allows it, they clock in right here.

341
00:24:43.884 --> 00:24:48.482
They can tell you how their week was, privately.

342
00:24:48.482 --> 00:24:51.739
Ask for a chat with their manager.

343
00:24:51.739 --> 00:24:55.380
And find someone to talk to, any time.

344
00:24:55.830 --> 00:24:59.462
The rota tab shows their next two weeks.

345
00:24:59.462 --> 00:25:01.460
Hours, rest, days off.

346
00:25:01.460 --> 00:25:09.543
Ben's not been given anything yet, but once the week's out, each shift appears here, with

347
00:25:09.543 --> 00:25:11.814
who they're working with.

348
00:25:12.265 --> 00:25:19.858
Requests is where they ask for holiday, time off, report sick, or say when they can

349
00:25:19.858 --> 00:25:20.316
work.

350
00:25:20.316 --> 00:25:22.969
A real say in their own rota.

351
00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:25.382
Pay shows their tips.

352
00:25:25.382 --> 00:25:30.428
And the inbox holds every message from their managers.

353
00:25:31.381 --> 00:25:33.436
So, that's Preshift Rota.

354
00:25:33.436 --> 00:25:36.725
A rota built from your forecast.

355
00:25:36.725 --> 00:25:39.910
Fair to the people who work it.

356
00:25:39.910 --> 00:25:42.479
Legal before it goes out.

357
00:25:42.479 --> 00:25:46.590
And costed the way payroll will cost it.

358
00:25:46.590 --> 00:25:48.748
Look after your team.

359
00:25:48.748 --> 00:25:52.653
and the numbers look after themselves.

360
00:25:52.653 --> 00:25:54.709
Thanks for watching.
